  The bridge runs inside this app on an ephemeral loopback port, and the
  webview reaches it over plain http://127.0.0.1. Android blocks cleartext by
  default from API 28 on, and Tauri's release build says so explicitly with
  android:usesCleartextTraffic="false" — so without this file every provider
  call through the bridge fails with ERR_CLEARTEXT_NOT_PERMITTED.

  Loopback is the one place where cleartext costs nothing: the traffic never
  leaves the device, and it is this app talking to itself. Everything else
  keeps the platform default and stays HTTPS-only.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" />
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">127.0.0.1</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">localhost</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
